  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nA broad trough situated over southern Canada and the northern \nU.S. will keep temperatures slightly below normal across \nsoutheast Oregon and southwest Idaho Sunday into early next \nweek. This pattern will promote afternoon instability and bring \na 25-40% chance of daily showers through Tuesday, primarily over\nhigher terrain. As the trough shifts eastward mid-week, the air\nmass over the forecast area will begin to modify as weak \nridging simultaneously builds to the west. Conditions should \ntrend warmer and drier during this transition, with temperatures\nclimbing to around 5 degrees above seasonal normals by \nThursday.",
